Sync the acrostic tracks and the trimmed lyrics.json from the working drive

Found while looking for the Heal Yourself videos: notes/lucky-sevens/lyrics.json
in this repo is behind your working copy on the Demosthenes drive, and the
acrostic assets are not here at all.

The repo copy runs to 550.838 and carries the closing acrostic as ordinary lyric
lines. Yours stops at 502.723 and hands the last 48.1 seconds to twelve separate
per-letter tracks, each starting on its own line and running to the end of the
song — so the letters appear one at a time and STAY, stacking into the two
columns. That is the ending as the production notes describe it, and it cannot be
expressed as a lyric line, because a lyric line ends.

    WDYNWTBF-1.1-W   502.723 -> 550.838   "W"
    WDYNWTBF-1.2-D   505.607 -> 550.838   "D"
    WDYNWTBF-1.3-Y   507.791 -> 550.838   "Y"
    WDYNWTBF-1.4-N   511.499 -> 550.838   "N"
    WDYNWTBF-1.5-q   515.536 -> 550.838   "¿"
    WDYNWTBF-2.1-W   527.101 -> 550.838   "W"   ... and so on for T, B, F, ¿

I checked before assuming: I first read the shorter file as a truncation, since
it is newer by mtime and missing the whole ending. It is not — the per-letter
files account for exactly the span it drops, and every entry in your copy also
exists in the repo copy, so nothing was lost, only moved.

So this takes your lyrics.json as the source of truth and adds the twelve
acrostic tracks under notes/lucky-sevens/acrostic/. spans.json and links.json
already matched byte for byte and are untouched.

Not copied: the file named "WDYN WTBF" with no extension. It holds the same ten
spans as WDYNWTBF-1.json but differs in content, and I would rather you tell me
which one is the keeper than guess and enshrine the wrong one.

Unrelated: tools/wayback-standalone is sitting untracked in the working tree. Not
mine and not touched here, but you may want it committed or ignored.
